\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The five regions of Section~\ref {sec:e3}. Each row is one region. ``Distance'' is the distance $d(c,c_i)$ between a request $c$ and an anchor $c_i$ that the score averages; ``compares'' says what this distance looks at; ``runs the model'' says whether scoring a request requires the generator; ``tuned over'' lists the adaptive weights (K, N, X, defined in the paragraph on weights) and the parameters among which the tuning pool chooses. Notation: $\mathbf  {e}(c)$ is the mean of the Gemma-2 hidden states of the prompt $c$ ($2304$ numbers); $S_\rho $ is the covariance $S$ of the approved embeddings of the tuning pool plus $\rho \operatorname  {tr}(S)/2304$ times the identity; $v(x_\ell ;c)$ is the guided velocity of $c$ at the noise end on the probe $x_\ell $ (a latent of $8192$ numbers); $\chi $ maps a decoded image to its CLIP ViT-L/14 embedding (unit norm, $768$ numbers). The parameters are tuned over $\rho \in \{10^{-4},10^{-2},10^{-1},1\}$ and $r\in \{0.62, 0.7, 0.75\}$.}}{33}{table.caption.71}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:e3_regions}{{11}{33}{The five regions of Section~\ref {sec:e3}. Each row is one region. ``Distance'' is the distance $d(c,c_i)$ between a request $c$ and an anchor $c_i$ that the score averages; ``compares'' says what this distance looks at; ``runs the model'' says whether scoring a request requires the generator; ``tuned over'' lists the adaptive weights (K, N, X, defined in the paragraph on weights) and the parameters among which the tuning pool chooses. Notation: $\be (c)$ is the mean of the Gemma-2 hidden states of the prompt $c$ ($2304$ numbers); $S_\rho $ is the covariance $S$ of the approved embeddings of the tuning pool plus $\rho \operatorname {tr}(S)/2304$ times the identity; $v(x_\ell ;c)$ is the guided velocity of $c$ at the noise end on the probe $x_\ell $ (a latent of $8192$ numbers); $\chi $ maps a decoded image to its CLIP ViT-L/14 embedding (unit norm, $768$ numbers). The parameters are tuned over $\rho \in \{10^{-4},10^{-2},10^{-1},1\}$ and $r\in \{\ethTRlevels \}$}{table.caption.71}{}}
